 "captions": [
  {
   "from": 23,
   "to": 72,
   "text": "In the year 793, England's chroniclers recorded something"
  },
  {
   "from": 73,
   "to": 88,
   "text": "terrifying."
  },
  {
   "from": 90,
   "to": 168,
   "text": "\"Immense sheets of light rushing through the air, and"
  },
  {
   "from": 169,
   "to": 261,
   "text": "whirlwinds, and fiery dragons flying across the firmament.\""
  },
  {
   "from": 263,
   "to": 327,
   "text": "Soon after, the Vikings came."
  },
  {
   "from": 328,
   "to": 398,
   "text": "They struck the holy island of Lindisfarne, and"
  },
  {
   "from": 399,
   "to": 480,
   "text": "the chronicle remembered those dragons as a warning."
  },
  {
   "from": 482,
   "to": 593,
   "text": "So what did medieval people actually believe a dragon was?"
  },
  {
   "from": 595,
   "to": 674,
   "text": "The answer is stranger than any movie."
  },
  {
   "from": 943,
   "to": 1030,
   "text": "The word comes from the Latin \"draco\", a giant serpent."
  },
  {
   "from": 1032,
   "to": 1054,
   "text": "Around the year 600,"
  },
  {
   "from": 1056,
   "to": 1148,
   "text": "Isidore of Seville wrote the encyclopedia that medieval"
  },
  {
   "from": 1150,
   "to": 1218,
   "text": "Europe trusted most after the Bible."
  },
  {
   "from": 1219,
   "to": 1297,
   "text": "His dragon was the largest creature on Earth."
  },
  {
   "from": 1299,
   "to": 1365,
   "text": "It had a crest and a small mouth, and"
  },
  {
   "from": 1366,
   "to": 1429,
   "text": "its power was not in its teeth."
  },
  {
   "from": 1431,
   "to": 1462,
   "text": "It was in its tail."
  },
  {
   "from": 1463,
   "to": 1557,
   "text": "The bestiaries, the illustrated animal books of the twelfth and"
  },
  {
   "from": 1558,
   "to": 1597,
   "text": "thirteenth centuries, added the details."
  },
  {
   "from": 1599,
   "to": 1675,
   "text": "A dragon waited on the paths elephants used,"
  },
  {
   "from": 1676,
   "to": 1740,
   "text": "knotted its tail around their legs, and"
  },
  {
   "from": 1741,
   "to": 1804,
   "text": "squeezed until they suffocated."
  },
  {
   "from": 1806,
   "to": 1891,
   "text": "It feared one animal above all: the panther,"
  },
  {
   "from": 1892,
   "to": 1965,
   "text": "whose sweet breath drew every creature to it,"
  },
  {
   "from": 1967,
   "to": 2042,
   "text": "except the dragon, which fled into hiding."
  },
  {
   "from": 2044,
   "to": 2128,
   "text": "And in these books, the dragon did not breathe fire."
  },
  {
   "from": 2130,
   "to": 2176,
   "text": "It didn't need to."
  },
  {
   "from": 2280,
   "to": 2331,
   "text": "The fire came from the poets."
  },
  {
   "from": 2333,
   "to": 2430,
   "text": "In Beowulf, a thief steals a jewelled cup from a dragon"
  },
  {
   "from": 2431,
   "to": 2540,
   "text": "sleeping on its treasure inside an ancient burial mound."
  },
  {
   "from": 2542,
   "to": 2618,
   "text": "The dragon wakes, and it burns the land,"
  },
  {
   "from": 2619,
   "to": 2668,
   "text": "the king's own hall included."
  },
  {
   "from": 2669,
   "to": 2735,
   "text": "The old king goes out to face it."
  },
  {
   "from": 2737,
   "to": 2774,
   "text": "His sword shatters."
  },
  {
   "from": 2775,
   "to": 2805,
   "text": "His men run."
  },
  {
   "from": 2806,
   "to": 2872,
   "text": "Only young Wiglaf stays beside him."
  },
  {
   "from": 2873,
   "to": 2997,
   "text": "Together they kill the dragon, but Beowulf dies of his wounds."
  },
  {
   "from": 2998,
   "to": 3074,
   "text": "It's often called medieval Europe's first fire-breathing"
  },
  {
   "from": 3075,
   "to": 3196,
   "text": "dragon, and the poem survives in exactly one manuscript."
  },
  {
   "from": 3197,
   "to": 3292,
   "text": "In 1731 that manuscript was caught in a library fire."
  },
  {
   "from": 3293,
   "to": 3368,
   "text": "You can still see where its edges burned."
  },
  {
   "from": 3369,
   "to": 3432,
   "text": "Further north, the Norse told of F\u00e1fnir,"
  },
  {
   "from": 3434,
   "to": 3526,
   "text": "so greedy for cursed gold that he killed his own father and"
  },
  {
   "from": 3527,
   "to": 3576,
   "text": "became a serpent coiled on it."
  },
  {
   "from": 3578,
   "to": 3632,
   "text": "The hero Sigurd hid in a pit and"
  },
  {
   "from": 3633,
   "to": 3699,
   "text": "stabbed upward as the dragon passed."
  },
  {
   "from": 3700,
   "to": 3788,
   "text": "When he roasted its heart and licked his burned finger,"
  },
  {
   "from": 3789,
   "to": 3868,
   "text": "he could suddenly understand the birds."
  },
  {
   "from": 3969,
   "to": 4054,
   "text": "For the Church, the dragon was the Devil himself."
  },
  {
   "from": 4056,
   "to": 4136,
   "text": "The Book of Revelation describes a great red dragon with"
  },
  {
   "from": 4137,
   "to": 4247,
   "text": "seven heads, thrown out of heaven by the archangel Michael."
  },
  {
   "from": 4248,
   "to": 4290,
   "text": "Then there's Saint George."
  },
  {
   "from": 4291,
   "to": 4388,
   "text": "The real George was a Roman soldier who died around the"
  },
  {
   "from": 4390,
   "to": 4400,
   "text": "year 303."
  },
  {
   "from": 4402,
   "to": 4494,
   "text": "His dragon didn't join the story for roughly seven hundred"
  },
  {
   "from": 4495,
   "to": 4511,
   "text": "years."
  },
  {
   "from": 4512,
   "to": 4597,
   "text": "The famous version comes from the Golden Legend,"
  },
  {
   "from": 4599,
   "to": 4634,
   "text": "written in the 1260s."
  },
  {
   "from": 4635,
   "to": 4747,
   "text": "Outside a city called Silene, a dragon was fed sheep, then"
  },
  {
   "from": 4748,
   "to": 4823,
   "text": "people, then children chosen by lottery,"
  },
  {
   "from": 4825,
   "to": 4886,
   "text": "until the lot fell on the king's daughter."
  },
  {
   "from": 4887,
   "to": 4958,
   "text": "George wounded the beast with his lance, and"
  },
  {
   "from": 4959,
   "to": 5083,
   "text": "the princess led it into the city on her belt, like a tame dog."
  },
  {
   "from": 5084,
   "to": 5183,
   "text": "Afterwards, it took four ox-carts to drag the body away."
  },
  {
   "from": 5185,
   "to": 5271,
   "text": "The same book tells of a saint who escaped from inside a"
  },
  {
   "from": 5273,
   "to": 5296,
   "text": "dragon's belly."
  },
  {
   "from": 5298,
   "to": 5387,
   "text": "Its own author called that story nonsense."
  },
  {
   "from": 5488,
   "to": 5556,
   "text": "Dragons flew over battlefields too."
  },
  {
   "from": 5558,
   "to": 5657,
   "text": "Roman cavalry rode behind dragon-shaped banners that hissed"
  },
  {
   "from": 5659,
   "to": 5681,
   "text": "in the wind."
  },
  {
   "from": 5683,
   "to": 5711,
   "text": "On the Bayeux Tapestry,"
  },
  {
   "from": 5712,
   "to": 5821,
   "text": "a dragon standard falls beside King Harold at Hastings, in 1066."
  },
  {
   "from": 5822,
   "to": 5891,
   "text": "In a history written in Wales around 830,"
  },
  {
   "from": 5892,
   "to": 5946,
   "text": "a king's tower keeps collapsing,"
  },
  {
   "from": 5947,
   "to": 6037,
   "text": "because two dragons are fighting in a pool beneath it:"
  },
  {
   "from": 6038,
   "to": 6137,
   "text": "a red one for the Britons, and a white one for the Saxons."
  },
  {
   "from": 6138,
   "to": 6199,
   "text": "A boy prophesies that the red will win."
  },
  {
   "from": 6200,
   "to": 6293,
   "text": "Henry Tudor carried that red dragon at Bosworth in 1485,"
  },
  {
   "from": 6294,
   "to": 6393,
   "text": "though it only became the official flag of Wales in 1959."
  },
  {
   "from": 6394,
   "to": 6470,
   "text": "In Poland, the oldest tale of the Wawel Dragon,"
  },
  {
   "from": 6471,
   "to": 6549,
   "text": "from around 1200, has two princes kill it with a cattle"
  },
  {
   "from": 6550,
   "to": 6611,
   "text": "hide stuffed with burning sulphur."
  },
  {
   "from": 6613,
   "to": 6725,
   "text": "Then one prince murders his brother, to take the credit."
  },
  {
   "from": 6829,
   "to": 6887,
   "text": "People also thought they had proof."
  },
  {
   "from": 6889,
   "to": 6976,
   "text": "Around 1335, a huge skull was dug out of a gravel pit near"
  },
  {
   "from": 6977,
   "to": 7012,
   "text": "Klagenfurt, in Austria, and"
  },
  {
   "from": 7014,
   "to": 7091,
   "text": "put on display in the town hall as a dragon's skull."
  },
  {
   "from": 7093,
   "to": 7142,
   "text": "In 1840 it was identified."
  },
  {
   "from": 7143,
   "to": 7208,
   "text": "It belonged to a woolly rhinoceros."
  },
  {
   "from": 7209,
   "to": 7282,
   "text": "The city's stone dragon, carved in the 1590s,"
  },
  {
   "from": 7284,
   "to": 7340,
   "text": "may even have been modelled on it."
  },
  {
   "from": 7341,
   "to": 7395,
   "text": "In the Czech city of Brno,"
  },
  {
   "from": 7397,
   "to": 7472,
   "text": "a dragon still hangs in the old town hall."
  },
  {
   "from": 7473,
   "to": 7537,
   "text": "It's a stuffed Nile crocodile."
  },
  {
   "from": 7538,
   "to": 7613,
   "text": "And in Krak\u00f3w, giant bones hang on a chain outside the"
  },
  {
   "from": 7615,
   "to": 7655,
   "text": "cathedral door."
  },
  {
   "from": 7754,
   "to": 7829,
   "text": "Medieval maps did show dragons,"
  },
  {
   "from": 7831,
   "to": 7909,
   "text": "sometimes coiled beneath the whole world."
  },
  {
   "from": 7910,
   "to": 7988,
   "text": "But the famous phrase \"here be dragons\" appears on exactly"
  },
  {
   "from": 7989,
   "to": 8087,
   "text": "one known object: a copper globe about the size of a"
  },
  {
   "from": 8088,
   "to": 8149,
   "text": "grapefruit, from the early 1500s."
  },
  {
   "from": 8150,
   "to": 8259,
   "text": "Off the coast of Asia, it reads, in Latin, \"Hic sunt dracones\"."
  },
  {
   "from": 8260,
   "to": 8288,
   "text": "Here are dragons."
  },
  {
   "from": 8289,
   "to": 8389,
   "text": "In 1855, an architect bought it in Paris for almost nothing,"
  },
  {
   "from": 8390,
   "to": 8458,
   "text": "and let his children play with it."
  },
  {
   "from": 8468,
   "to": 8543,
   "text": "So a medieval dragon was many things."
  },
  {
   "from": 8544,
   "to": 8584,
   "text": "A light in the sky."
  },
  {
   "from": 8585,
   "to": 8627,
   "text": "A skull in the gravel."
  },
  {
   "from": 8628,
   "to": 8689,
   "text": "A crocodile from far away."
  },
  {
   "from": 8691,
   "to": 8728,
   "text": "The Devil himself."
  },
  {
   "from": 8729,
   "to": 8819,
   "text": "Most of all, it was the shape people gave to everything"
  },
  {
   "from": 8820,
   "to": 8859,
   "text": "they couldn't explain."
  },
  {
   "from": 8861,
   "to": 8917,
   "text": "If you enjoyed this, subscribe."
  },
  {
   "from": 8918,
   "to": 8983,
   "text": "There are more legends to come."
  }
 ],
 "sfx": []
}